WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.909
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book three.

2
00:00:05.209 --> 00:00:09.071
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.371 --> 00:00:15.437
Unit three: Social Responsibility. Today you will talk about past mistakes with 'should have'.

4
00:00:15.737 --> 00:00:18.331
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:22.604
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:24.985
Ethical obligation.

7
00:00:25.983 --> 00:00:29.202
Ethical obligation means a duty to do what is right.

8
00:00:29.817 --> 00:00:32.048
We have an ethical obligation to help.

9
00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:35.941
Your turn. Say: Ethical obligation.

10
00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:40.300
Ethical obligation.

11
00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:42.411
Community impact.

12
00:00:43.417 --> 00:00:46.926
Community impact means the effect something has on local people.

13
00:00:47.517 --> 00:00:50.166
The new factory had a big community impact.

14
00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:53.809
Your turn. Say: Community impact.

15
00:00:56.667 --> 00:00:58.074
Community impact.

16
00:00:58.817 --> 00:01:00.456
Corporate responsibility.

17
00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:05.446
Corporate responsibility means a company's duty to society and nature.

18
00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:09.083
Corporate responsibility means fair pay and clean air.

19
00:01:09.683 --> 00:01:12.800
Your turn. Say: Corporate responsibility.

20
00:01:15.667 --> 00:01:17.515
Corporate responsibility.

21
00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:19.669
Social contract.

22
00:01:20.683 --> 00:01:24.564
Social contract means an unwritten agreement to live well together.

23
00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:27.846
Paying taxes is part of the social contract.

24
00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:31.567
Your turn. Say: Social contract.

25
00:01:34.433 --> 00:01:36.027
Social contract.

26
00:01:36.783 --> 00:01:38.098
Collective action.

27
00:01:39.083 --> 00:01:42.232
Collective action means people working together for a goal.

28
00:01:42.817 --> 00:01:45.083
Collective action cleaned the whole beach.

29
00:01:45.683 --> 00:01:48.370
Your turn. Say: Collective action.

30
00:01:51.233 --> 00:01:52.606
Collective action.

31
00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:54.432
Public good.

32
00:01:55.417 --> 00:01:57.915
Public good means something that helps everyone.

33
00:01:58.517 --> 00:02:00.261
Clean water is a public good.

34
00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:03.351
Your turn. Say: Public good.

35
00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:07.248
Public good.

36
00:02:07.983 --> 00:02:09.170
Accountability.

37
00:02:10.183 --> 00:02:13.843
Accountability means accepting responsibility for your actions.

38
00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:16.241
Leaders need accountability.

39
00:02:16.850 --> 00:02:20.013
Your turn. Say: Accountability.

40
00:02:22.867 --> 00:02:24.135
Accountability.

41
00:02:24.883 --> 00:02:26.070
Moral duty.

42
00:02:27.083 --> 00:02:30.116
Moral duty means something you should do because it is right.

43
00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:33.192
Helping the injured is a moral duty.

44
00:02:33.783 --> 00:02:37.063
Your turn. Say: Moral duty.

45
00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:41.087
Moral duty.

46
00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:43.594
Sustainable practice.

47
00:02:44.583 --> 00:02:48.278
Sustainable practice means a way of working that protects the future.

48
00:02:48.883 --> 00:02:51.301
Recycling is a sustainable practice.

49
00:02:51.917 --> 00:02:55.057
Your turn. Say: Sustainable practice.

50
00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:00.155
Sustainable practice.

51
00:03:00.917 --> 00:03:02.510
Shared responsibility.

52
00:03:03.517 --> 00:03:06.967
Shared responsibility means a duty that everyone has together.

53
00:03:07.583 --> 00:03:10.372
A clean school is a shared responsibility.

54
00:03:10.983 --> 00:03:14.657
Your turn. Say: Shared responsibility.

55
00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:19.302
Shared responsibility.

56
00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:21.121
Civic virtue.

57
00:03:22.117 --> 00:03:24.766
Civic virtue means good behaviour as a citizen.

58
00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:27.396
Volunteering shows civic virtue.

59
00:03:27.983 --> 00:03:30.705
Your turn. Say: Civic virtue.

60
00:03:33.567 --> 00:03:34.812
Civic virtue.

61
00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:36.748
Global impact.

62
00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:40.585
Global impact means an effect on the whole world.

63
00:03:41.183 --> 00:03:43.612
Plastic pollution has a global impact.

64
00:03:44.217 --> 00:03:47.461
Your turn. Say: Global impact.

65
00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:51.510
Global impact.

66
00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:55.928
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:56.783 --> 00:04:00.550
Visal, the river near your village is polluted. What happened?

68
00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:06.090
Factories dumped waste. We should have acted sooner to protect the community.

69
00:04:07.183 --> 00:04:08.684
What should people have done?

70
00:04:09.783 --> 00:04:14.233
The factory should have followed the rules, and we should have reported it.

71
00:04:15.317 --> 00:04:16.353
And now?

72
00:04:17.450 --> 00:04:22.645
Now we are taking collective action. It is a shared responsibility.

73
00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:25.370
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:26.217 --> 00:04:28.785
Grammar focus: Modal perfect (should have).

75
00:04:29.085 --> 00:04:30.318
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:31.017 --> 00:04:32.621
We should have acted sooner.

77
00:04:33.517 --> 00:04:35.493
The company shouldn't have dumped waste.

78
00:04:36.383 --> 00:04:37.756
I should have reported it.

79
00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:43.927
Use 'should have' + past participle to talk about a past action that was the right thing but didn't happen.

80
00:04:44.683 --> 00:04:47.939
Be careful! Don't say: We should acted sooner.

81
00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:52.016
Say: We should have acted sooner.

82
00:04:52.316 --> 00:04:54.431
Say 'should have' + past participle.

83
00:04:55.233 --> 00:04:57.955
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:58.767 --> 00:04:59.954
Doing Our Part.

85
00:05:00.254 --> 00:05:03.472
Social responsibility is a shared responsibility.

86
00:05:04.467 --> 00:05:08.022
When a river is polluted, we often say we should have acted sooner.

87
00:05:09.033 --> 00:05:12.751
Companies have corporate responsibility for their community impact.

88
00:05:13.767 --> 00:05:16.776
Citizens show civic virtue through collective action.

89
00:05:17.767 --> 00:05:20.985
Small sustainable practices can have a global impact.

90
00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:26.462
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:27.317 --> 00:05:29.061
We should have blank sooner.

92
00:05:29.361 --> 00:05:32.318
A, acted. B, act. C, acting.

93
00:05:35.867 --> 00:05:37.843
The answer is A: acted.

94
00:05:38.983 --> 00:05:41.552
Something that helps everyone is a public blank.

95
00:05:41.852 --> 00:05:45.377
A, good. B, duty. C, contract.

96
00:05:48.933 --> 00:05:50.619
The answer is A: good.

97
00:05:51.783 --> 00:05:54.549
People working together for a goal is blank action.

98
00:05:54.849 --> 00:05:58.212
A, collective. B, moral. C, global.

99
00:06:01.767 --> 00:06:03.987
The answer is A: collective.

100
00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:08.166
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:06:09.017 --> 00:06:12.676
What social responsibility do you feel toward your community?

102
00:06:21.483 --> 00:06:22.902
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:23.202 --> 00:06:32.937
I feel responsible for keeping my village clean. Last year we should have started earlier, but now I organise a clean-up every month.

104
00:06:33.237 --> 00:06:34.911
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:35.817 --> 00:06:40.280
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and modal perfect (should have).

106
00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:45.775
Today's value is civic responsibility. Take care of your city, because it is everyone's home.

107
00:06:46.075 --> 00:06:48.635
See you in Unit four. Goodbye!

108
00:06:48.935 --> 00:06:52.667
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

